# SHA-256 of every upstream file this SDK ships unmodified from the official
# simdjson 5.0.2 release tarball.
#
#   https://codeload.github.com/simdjson/simdjson/tar.gz/refs/tags/v5.0.2
#   tag v5.0.2, tag commit c9030726ebbf5f9fe9f9facb4a401f6d3ccd77a2
#   released 2026-10-04 (committer date of that tag), 8331647 bytes
#   sha256 09de4289a26d3a0453569901a3837450b5b98a5c317d635eeee8e2a82b1ebe6b
#
# 771 records under src/, 10317170 bytes: the complete extracted
# tarball tree except the three files listed below. That includes every header
# under src/include/simdjson/, every per-architecture kernel under
# src/src/, upstream's own test suite under src/tests/, its documentation under
# src/doc/, its benchmarks, fuzzers, tools and CMake tree, the json examples
# under src/jsonexamples/, and both licence texts. Nothing is dropped for being
# uncompiled: the Zig build reads src/src/simdjson.cpp, src/include/ and the
# include path src/src/, and nothing else in this list, but a dependent receives
# upstream's project rather than a hand-picked subset of it.
#
# Three files of the tarball are deliberately absent and are recorded as absent
# rather than omitted quietly. They are upstream's *generated* single-header
# amalgamation -- the output of src/singleheader/amalgamate.py, which is itself
# carried here and unmodified:
#
#   src/singleheader/simdjson.h
#   src/singleheader/simdjson.cpp
#   src/singleheader/singleheader.zip
#
# Their absence is the package's whole point: this build compiles upstream's own
# src/src/simdjson.cpp translation unit directly, so an amalgamated copy of the
# same sources sitting beside it would be a second, buildable, drifting copy of
# the upstream core with nothing keeping the two in step. The generator that
# makes them is present, so the amalgamation is reproducible on demand rather
# than stale. tools/check-provenance.sh fails if any of the three reappears.
# See UPSTREAM.md, "The generated amalgamation is deliberately not shipped".
#
# The last 22 records are this package's own test fixtures under
# testdata/, totalling 645673 bytes. They are not upstream files: they are
# either transcribed from RFC 8259, copied from upstream's own
# src/jsonexamples/twitter.json, or authored by this fork for a specific
# behaviour. Their provenance, their selection and the reason each one exists are
# recorded in UPSTREAM.md, "The test fixtures", and the fork-authored ones are
# described individually there.
#
# `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` from the repository root checks the bytes.
# tools/check-provenance.sh additionally rejects a missing, extra or renamed
# file under src/, rejects the three generated amalgamation files reappearing,
# rejects README.upstream.md drifting from src/README.md, and rejects the
# release digest here and in UPSTREAM.md disagreeing.
